  "title": "Red Bull's Cans Circle Earth 23 Times",
  "name_card": "What if you lined up every Red Bull can",
  "name_sub": "one year of cans around Earth",
  "description": "What if you lined up every Red Bull can sold in one year, side by side, around the Earth? Red Bull says 13.969 billion cans were sold worldwide in 2025. Our math: we used a standard can, 6.6 centimeters wide at its widest point (Wikipedia, the US standard can; Red Bull's 8.4 fl oz can is slimmer, so the real line would be shorter). 13.969 billion x 6.6 cm = about 922,000 km. Earth's circumference is about 40,075 km (Wikipedia). 922,000 / 40,075 = about 23 trips around. This is simple made-up math for fun, not a Red Bull claim.\n\nSources:\n- Red Bull: How many cans does Red Bull sell worldwide?: https://www.redbull.com/us-en/energydrink/how-many-cans-does-red-bull-sell-world-wide\n- Wikipedia: Beverage can: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beverage_can\n- Wikipedia: Earth: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth\n\n#shorts #redbull #whatif #howtheymakemoney",
